1. THE "HOW-TO" (Environment & Setup)
A. Fixing PAC CLI Path Mismatches

Problem: VS Code may prioritize a broken internal CLI version over the system version.

Action: 1. Always verify paths using where.exe pac in both Windows Terminal and VS Code.
2. If VS Code fails while the system terminal works, manually point the VS Code "Power Platform: PAC Location" setting to: C:\Users\IT Dev\AppData\Local\Microsoft\PowerAppsCLI.
3. If the extension's "bolt" module is missing, delete the pac folder in %AppData%\Roaming\Code\User\globalStorage\microsoft-isvexptools.powerplatform-vscode\ and restart.

B. Fixing Terminal Rendering (Encoding)

Problem: PAC commands output weird symbols like ΓöÇ.

Action: Force UTF-8 encoding.

Command: [Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8

Permanent Fix: Add $OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8 to your $PROFILE.

C. Project Commands

pac code run: Local test harness (Hosts code locally).

pac code push: Pushes current build to the Dataverse/Power Apps cloud.

npm start: Alternative to trigger the local watcher if pac wrapper is buggy.

2. KNOWN USER PREFERENCES (UI/UX Standards)
A. Visual Theme

Primary: Navy Blue

Background: White

Accent/Sub: Red

